      "text": "In 2024, Raskin’s Oversight staff used accounting records to document at least $7.8 million in payments from 20 foreign governments to four Trump businesses during his first presidency. The payments raised questions about foreign governments spending money at properties owned by a sitting president. Whether any government received favorable treatment in return is a separate question. Raskin’s staff also said further production of Trump accounting records stopped after Comer took over the committee in 2023. If Comer wants Democrats to defend their record on the Biden inquiry, he should be prepared to explain what records he was willing to pursue when the subject was Trump."
